{"id":"p09-l01","minutes":35,"summary":"Every electric actuator rests on two laws. A current in a magnetic field feels a force, and a conductor moving through a field generates a voltage. You derive both for a coil in a magnet gap, show that the force constant and the back-EMF constant are the same number, and compute the force on a voice coil that partly leaves its gap.","html":"<h2 id=\"force-on-a-current-lorentz\">Force on a current: Lorentz</h2>\n<p>A straight conductor of length <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> carrying current <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span> across a uniform field <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span></span></span></span> feels</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7694em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8805em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>so when <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⊥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span></span></span></span> the magnitude is</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>The direction follows the right-hand rule: fingers along the current, bend them toward <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span></span></span></span>, and the thumb gives the force. A coil of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> turns, each with active length <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> in the field, gives</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>so force is <strong>linear in current</strong>. That linearity is why a current loop (lesson 7) is really a torque or force loop.</p>\n<p>In a <strong>voice-coil actuator</strong> (loudspeaker, hard-disk head, a lens focus motor), a radial field crosses a cylindrical gap and the coil sits in it. Each turn has active length <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span>, and every element sees <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">B</span></span></span></span> perpendicular to it, so the forces add axially.</p>\n<h2 id=\"voltage-from-motion-faraday\">Voltage from motion: Faraday</h2>\n<p>When the coil moves at speed <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span>, each turn sweeps flux at the rate <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">Lv</span></span></span></span>, and Faraday’s law <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord\">Φ/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span></span></span></span> gives a <strong>back-EMF</strong></p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>The two constants are the same number, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>, in N/A and V·s/m (which are the same unit). That’s not a coincidence but energy conservation: the electrical power absorbed by the back-EMF, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span>, equals the mechanical power delivered, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">Lv</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>For rotary motors the same argument gives torque <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span> and back-EMF <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span></span></span></span>, with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> in SI units (lesson 2).</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-the-coil-leaves-the-gap\">When the coil leaves the gap</h2>\n<p>The field is only strong inside the gap. Outside it falls off over a fringe of a few millimetres. If the coil is longer than the gap (“overhung”), the number of turns in the field stays constant over a stroke and the force constant stays flat; if it moves past that, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> drops. Datasheets give a force-versus-stroke curve for exactly this reason.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"lorentz\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Three conductors of a coil in the gap between two magnet poles. The force (lime) is proportional to current, field and turns, and reverses with the current.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A voice coil has <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span></span></span></span> turns of radius 4.77 mm (so each turn is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">30</span></span></span></span> mm long) in a 0.8 T radial gap.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Force constant: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.8</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.030</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.2</span></span></span></span> N/A.</li>\n<li>At 2 A: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.4</span></span></span></span> N.</li>\n<li>Moving at 0.5 m/s, the back-EMF is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span></span></span></span> V.</li>\n<li>Power check: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.2</span></span></span></span> W, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.4</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.2</span></span></span></span> W.</li>\n<li>With 4 Ω of coil resistance, holding 2.4 N still costs <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">16</span></span></span></span> W of heat. Force from a coil is cheap to make and expensive to hold.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">voice_coil.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">gap_field</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">z, B0=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>, h=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.006</span>, fringe=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0015</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Radial flux density at axial position z: flat in the gap of height h, Gaussian fringe outside.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    over = np.maximum(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(z) - h / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> B0 * np.exp(-(over / fringe) ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">coil_force</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">I, z0, N=<span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>, r=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.030</span> / (<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi</span>), coil_len=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.004</span>, segs=<span class=\"hljs-number\">360</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Sum I dl x B over every turn and segment. Radial B, tangential dl -&gt; axial force.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    zs = z0 + np.linspace(-coil_len / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, coil_len / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, N)      <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># turn positions</span>\n    phi = np.linspace(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi, segs, endpoint=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>)\n    dphi = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi / segs\n    F = np.zeros(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> z <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> zs:\n        B = gap_field(z)\n        dl = np.stack([-np.sin(phi), np.cos(phi), np.zeros_like(phi)], <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * r * dphi\n        Bv = np.stack([np.cos(phi), np.sin(phi), np.zeros_like(phi)], <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * B\n        F += I * np.cross(dl, Bv).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> F\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    F = coil_force(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;force at 2 A, centred:&quot;</span>, np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(F, <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(F[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(F[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># radial parts cancel</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(F[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.030</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># N B I L = 2.4 N</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># linear in current</span>\n    Is = np.linspace(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">11</span>)\n    Fz = np.array([coil_force(I, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> I <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> Is])\n    slope, icpt = np.polyfit(Is, Fz, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(Fz - slope * Is)) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(icpt) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># power balance: back-EMF e = k v, so e*I == F*v</span>\n    k = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(slope); v = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(k * v * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span> - <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(F[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]) * v) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># force falls once turns leave the 6 mm gap</span>\n    off = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(coil_force(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.004</span>)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;k_f = <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{k:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> N/A; force with the coil 4 mm off centre: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{off:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> N&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> off &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span> * <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(F[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A rotary motor’s datasheet gives a torque constant of 0.05 N·m/A. What back-EMF does it produce at 3000 rpm?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span></span></span></span> V·s/rad. At 3000 rpm, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">/60</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">314.2</span></span></span></span> rad/s, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15.7</span></span></span></span> V.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does a voice-coil actuator get hot when it holds a load against gravity but not when it moves freely?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Holding force needs a steady current, and with no motion all the electrical power <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span> becomes heat (the back-EMF is zero, so no power goes to mechanical work). Moving freely needs little current. This is why gravity-loaded voice coils use springs or counterweights.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p09-l01\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"force-on-a-current-lorentz","title":"Force on a current: Lorentz"},{"id":"voltage-from-motion-faraday","title":"Voltage from motion: Faraday"},{"id":"when-the-coil-leaves-the-gap","title":"When the coil leaves the gap"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p09-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Force constant in N/A for N = 50, B = 0.8 T, L = 0.03 m per turn?</p>\n","explain":"<p>k = N·B·L.</p>\n","answer":1.2,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N/A"},{"id":"p09-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Force in N on that coil at 2 A?</p>\n","explain":"<p>F = k·I.</p>\n","answer":2.4,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N"},{"id":"p09-l01-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Back-EMF in V at 0.5 m/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>e = k·v.</p>\n","answer":0.6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p09-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Back-EMF in V of a 0.05 N·m/A motor at 3000 rpm?</p>\n","explain":"<p>k_e = k_t in SI units.</p>\n","answer":15.71,"tol":0.002,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p09-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why is k_f equal to k_e?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Electrical power in equals mechanical power out.</p>\n","options":["by coincidence of units","energy conservation, e·I = F·v","only for voice coils","because B is uniform"],"answer":1},{"id":"p09-l01-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Reversing the current in the coil…</p>\n","explain":"<p>F = I L × B is linear in I.</p>\n","options":["leaves the force unchanged","reverses the force","doubles the force","removes the back-EMF"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"voice_coil.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndef gap_field(z, B0=0.8, h=0.006, fringe=0.0015):\n    \"\"\"Radial flux density at axial position z: flat in the gap of height h, Gaussian fringe outside.\"\"\"\n    over = np.maximum(np.abs(z) - h / 2, 0)\n    return B0 * np.exp(-(over / fringe) ** 2)\n\ndef coil_force(I, z0, N=50, r=0.030 / (2 * np.pi), coil_len=0.004, segs=360):\n    \"\"\"Sum I dl x B over every turn and segment. Radial B, tangential dl -> axial force.\"\"\"\n    zs = z0 + np.linspace(-coil_len / 2, coil_len / 2, N)      # turn positions\n    phi = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, segs, endpoint=False)\n    dphi = 2 * np.pi / segs\n    F = np.zeros(3)\n    for z in zs:\n        B = gap_field(z)\n        dl = np.stack([-np.sin(phi), np.cos(phi), np.zeros_like(phi)], 1) * r * dphi\n        Bv = np.stack([np.cos(phi), np.sin(phi), np.zeros_like(phi)], 1) * B\n        F += I * np.cross(dl, Bv).sum(0)\n    return F\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    F = coil_force(2.0, 0.0)\n    print(\"force at 2 A, centred:\", np.round(F, 6))\n    assert abs(F[0]) < 1e-9 and abs(F[1]) < 1e-9          # radial parts cancel\n    assert abs(abs(F[2]) - 50 * 0.8 * 2.0 * 0.030) < 1e-9    # N B I L = 2.4 N\n    # linear in current\n    Is = np.linspace(-5, 5, 11)\n    Fz = np.array([coil_force(I, 0.0)[2] for I in Is])\n    slope, icpt = np.polyfit(Is, Fz, 1)\n    assert np.max(np.abs(Fz - slope * Is)) < 1e-9 and abs(icpt) < 1e-9\n    # power balance: back-EMF e = k v, so e*I == F*v\n    k = abs(slope); v = 0.5\n    assert abs(k * v * 2.0 - abs(F[2]) * v) < 1e-12\n    # force falls once turns leave the 6 mm gap\n    off = abs(coil_force(2.0, 0.004)[2])\n    print(f\"k_f = {k:.3f} N/A; force with the coil 4 mm off centre: {off:.2f} N\")\n    assert off < 0.8 * abs(F[2])"}]}